From: GL-XE3000 OpenWrt port <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] add cjson.empty_array sentinel for forcing [] over {}

This vendored lua-cjson (upstream Mark Pulford 2.1.0, not the OpenResty
fork) has no way to encode a genuinely empty Lua table as JSON "[]" -
lua_array_length() returns 0 for `{}` (no non-integer keys were found,
so it's not rejected as an object, but there's nothing to report either),
and json_append_data()'s `if (len > 0)` check treats 0 the same as "not
an array", always falling through to json_append_object() and emitting
"{}".

This is a real, live bug in the GL-XE3000 OpenWrt port project: any RPC
handler returning an empty array-typed field (e.g. an empty client list)
serializes it as a JSON object, and the vendored GL frontend - unmodified,
calling plain Array methods like `.map()` on it - throws
"TypeError: e.map is not a function" and silently breaks the page.
Confirmed via live browser console errors while zero clients were
connected.

Fix: add `cjson.empty_array`, a single distinguished empty table stored
in the Lua registry. json_append_data() checks table identity against it
before running the normal array-length heuristic; on a match it emits
"[]" directly regardless of content. This is purely additive - every
other table (including every other empty `{}`) encodes exactly as
before. Lua code opts in explicitly per call site by returning
`cjson.empty_array` instead of `{}` where it means "empty array", the
same explicit-opt-in shape OpenResty's own cjson fork uses for its
`array_mt`/`empty_array` mechanism (this just doesn't need a metatable
check since a plain reference-equality check is enough for one sentinel
value).

--- a/lua_cjson.c
+++ b/lua_cjson.c
@@ -674,6 +674,14 @@ static void json_append_data(lua_State *l, json_config_t *cfg,
             strbuf_append_mem(json, "false", 5);
         break;
     case LUA_TTABLE:
+        /* GL SDK4 port: cjson.empty_array sentinel, forces "[]" */
+        lua_getfield(l, LUA_REGISTRYINDEX, "cjson.empty_array");
+        if (lua_rawequal(l, -1, -2)) {
+            lua_pop(l, 1);
+            strbuf_append_mem(json, "[]", 2);
+            break;
+        }
+        lua_pop(l, 1);
         current_depth++;
         json_check_encode_depth(l, cfg, current_depth, json);
         len = lua_array_length(l, cfg, json);
@@ -1371,6 +1379,21 @@ static int lua_cjson_new(lua_State *l)
     /* Set cjson.null */
     lua_pushlightuserdata(l, NULL);
     lua_setfield(l, -2, "null");
+
+    /* GL SDK4 port: cjson.empty_array, see json_append_data */
+    /*
+     * cjson and cjson.safe each call lua_cjson_new().  Reuse one registry
+     * sentinel instead of replacing it on the second module load, otherwise
+     * the first module's exported table stops comparing equal.
+     */
+    lua_getfield(l, LUA_REGISTRYINDEX, "cjson.empty_array");
+    if (lua_isnil(l, -1)) {
+        lua_pop(l, 1);
+        lua_newtable(l);
+        lua_pushvalue(l, -1);
+        lua_setfield(l, LUA_REGISTRYINDEX, "cjson.empty_array");
+    }
+    lua_setfield(l, -2, "empty_array");
 
     /* Set module name / version fields */
     lua_pushliteral(l, CJSON_MODNAME);
